      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this useful - which threads is mSupportedTypeBitmap accessed on ?\n\nvolatile is generally only useful when there\u0027s several threads accessing the var, and it\u0027s OK for each access (including subsequent accesses in one thread) to get inconsistent values. In particular you\u0027ve got code like this:\n\n        if (preSupportedBitmap !\u003d mSupportedTypeBitmap) {\n            reportTetheringSupportedChange(mSupportedTypeBitmap);\n        }\n        \nthat indicates that this is not the case (two subsequent accesses may see a different value if another thread is writing to the var, and so reportTetheringSupportedChange may be called with preSupportedBitmap)",
      "range": {
